    "title": "pandas.Index.drop — pandas 3.0.5 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Index.drop#\n\n- \nIndex.drop(*labels* ,*errors='raise'* )[source]#\n- Make new Index with passed list of labels deleted. \n  - Parameters:\n    - **labels** array-like or scalar\n    - Array-like object or a scalar value, representing the labels to be removed from the Index.\n    - **errors** {‘ignore’, ‘raise’}, default ‘raise’\n    - If ‘ignore’, suppress error and existing labels are dropped.\n  - Returns:\n    - Index\n    - Will be same type as self, except for RangeIndex.\n  - Raises:\n    - KeyError\n    - If not all of the labels are found in the selected axis\n See also \n  - `Index.dropna`\n  - Return Index without NA/NaN values.\n  - `Index.drop_duplicates`\n  - Return Index with duplicate values removed.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.Index([\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"]) >>> idx.drop([\"a\"]) Index(['b', 'c'], dtype='str')",
    "markdown_length": 812,
